{"ratings":[{"id":"F1","consequence":"nuisance","trigger":"unusual","reason":"A prolonged event-loop stall can allow two suites to run despite a limit of one, but the specified lease expiry permits the stalled owner to lose its slot and the evidence establishes only overlapping work."},{"id":"F2","consequence":"nuisance","trigger":"plausible","reason":"A restart while a client waits can lose its queue position and leave a phantom holder that delays its replacement until the lease expires."},{"id":"F3","consequence":"nuisance","trigger":"normal","reason":"Idle pools take write locks repeatedly by default, causing avoidable contention and transient responsiveness delays."}]}